<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Otieno rides a bicycle along a straight road that runs east to west. He rides <m>{5}</m> km east from his home to the market, then <m>{8}</m> km west to the posho mill.</p><p>(a) How far does he ride altogether?</p><div><fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/> km  </div><p>(b) How far is the posho mill from his home?</p><div><fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> km  </div><p>(c) In which direction is the posho mill from his home?</p><div>[ east | west ]  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Draw the road with home at the start. The first ride goes <m>{5}</m> km east; the second comes back <m>{8}</m> km west.</p><p>(a) The distance ridden counts every kilometre: <m>{5} + {8} = {13}</m> km.</p><p>(b) The displacement is where he ends up compared with where he started, in a straight line. He came back further than he went, so he ends <m>{8} - {5} = {3}</m> km from home, on the other side.</p><p>(c) West of home: the ride west was the longer one. Distance is a scalar; displacement, a size together with a direction, is a vector.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>13</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p>west</p></answer>
</stack-static>